Z||000001||grinthock||06-06-2001||07:17 AM||||Check out <BR> <A HREF="http://grinthock.2y.net/87gt.html" TARGET=_blank>http://grinthock.2y.net/87gt.html</A> <P>click on intake project, this is what i did on my V-6 I am sure something similar could be done on your L4||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroJoe||06-06-2001||09:21 AM||||Its only plastic, you can probably get at it with a cutter on a dremel or something.  If you are worried about breaking something, you can take it completely out by disconnection your intake hose, taking off your grill, taking off your plastic inner fender mud sheild, and then removing the air box itself.  Shouldnt take you too long, and that way you can get a better position to see inside of it.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/joesig_1.jpg"> <BR>'87 Coupe 5spd.<BR>AIM:FieroJoe87||||reg||1
Z||000003||Formula88||06-06-2001||09:24 AM||||I just removed mine.  I had to take out the fender liner, but it wasn't too hard.  I then ran a flexible intake duct fromt he bottom of the factory air cleaner (V6) to the vent on the fender.  Still uses the factory filter, but sounds much better.  And I don't have to change my filter in the fender!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
