Z||000005||DecadenceR||06-06-2001||03:26 PM||||Even though, according to that article, any air intake mods are pretty much useless, wouldn't removing the air restriction cause more airflow through the engine compartment and therefore help with cooling?<P>As far as I've seen, most of the mods, especially on the 6cyl, are similar to those in the imports. A tube with a filter on the end. So it's not like you directly feed the air like a stock 4 is supposed to. <P>This is just my method of thinking, so if I'm wrong please explain it to me.||||reg||1
Z||000006||theogre||06-06-2001||07:43 PM||||altering the airbox does nothing for cooling. The airbox is connected only to the engine air intake.||||reg||1
