Z||000016||Mach10||06-07-2001||09:59 PM||||About the stock air intake: I've seen the benchmarks, and the system is more than free-flowing enough for whatever that 2.8 can suck down. If you have a larger motor, or mods that would increase your air requirements, then you may be seeing some restriction. For me, I'd like to remove the water trap, mostly for the nifty sucking noises, but I'd rather not hydro-lock my motor, thanks.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||6
Z||000017||qwikgta||06-07-2001||10:09 PM||||Not sure if this helps at all but remember that "us" 4 cly DUKE guys have a diff type of fuel injector (TBI).  Because mine is shaped more like a old time carb i used old time idea with the open element filter.  With the 6 cly guys you have a side mounted throttle body with fuel injectors for each cylnder (MPFI) (not new info, I know).  SO I see how you could benefit from the RICE boy tube and filter idea.  I tryed to do it to my TBI but you cant bend a tube and fit under the hood/trunk.    Anyway, I don't know if it helps or hurts my engine, I have not driven it in HOT weather yet.  It does change the sound a lot.  And lets face it, it ain't no screamer of an engine anyway.  <P>Rob<P>------------------<BR>qwikgta@yahoo.com<BR>88 T-Top coupe, 65K, Header, 16" GTZ rims, short shifter, swaybar.<BR>http://robsfieroproject.homestead.com/index.html<BR>http://vafiero.com||||reg||1
Z||000018||hyhy4u||06-07-2001||11:22 PM||||I took out the whole "water thingy" thing out.  I dont tend to see much of a performance change under slow speeds but on the express way it seems to have a little more guts to it, not only that but it makes a whole wooshing noise when the cars on.||||reg||14
